# Redeploy challenges after changes

When you add or edit anything under `challenges/`, **finish by redeploying to local CTFd** (do not skip unless deploy fails and the user must fix infra).

From the repo root:

```sh
export GPG_PASSPHRASE='TESTING42'
export CTFD_TOKEN='ctfd_0cb2ccac1f05fd0d545f187bb21bed7a7a630eb974a47e6d2c76ce69f7736afa'

# Start CTFd if needed
sg docker -c "cd submodules/ctfd && docker compose --profile shell-1 up -d ctfd-shell-1"

python3 submodules/deploy_challenges/deploy_challenges.py \
  --no-clone . \
  --subdir challenges \
  --url http://localhost:9042/ctfd/default \
  --token "$CTFD_TOKEN" \
  --force
```

If flags were regenerated as plaintext, run `cd challenges && ./encrypt.sh` first (requires `GPG_PASSPHRASE`).

Report deploy success count (e.g. `34/34`) in your final message.
